  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: AppComm 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'Patients taking a newly approved cancer treatment report that it is
    helping, but some are starting to experience chronic fatigue and headaches. You
    bring these concerns to a community advisory meeting.


    <b>What role is the
    community advocate playing in this situation?</b>'
  explanation: Community advocates help amplify patient voices by sharing real-world
    experiences with researchers, clinicians, and advocacy groups. This helps identify
    patterns that may not have been seen in clinical trials. Their input supports
    ongoing safety monitoring and keeps patient needs visible, ensuring their concerns
    are addressed promptly.
  correctAnswer: Sharing real-world experiences to help identify safety trends
  incorrectAnswer1: Approving updates to the new treatment label
  incorrectAnswer2: Deciding whether the new treatment should stay on the market
  incorrectAnswer3: Recommending a new treatment dosage
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Approval
